            {
              "id": "secret.aws_access_key_id",
              "name": "SecretAwsAccessKeyId",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "AWS access key id"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An access key id in source usually sits next to its secret key, and it identifies the account to attackers."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Remove it, rotate the key pair in IAM, and load credentials from the environment, a credentials file or an IAM role.",
                "markdown": "**Why:** An access key id in source usually sits next to its secret key, and it identifies the account to attackers.\n\n**Fix:** Remove it, rotate the key pair in IAM, and load credentials from the environment, a credentials file or an IAM role."
