            {
              "id": "java.exec.command",
              "name": "JavaExecCommand",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Runtime.exec or ProcessBuilder with request data, Java and Kotlin"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Runtime.getRuntime().exec() and new ProcessBuilder() start the program they are given. A request value that chooses the program, or reaches the script of 'sh -c' or 'cmd /c', runs commands of the attacker's choosing; Runtime.exec(String) also splits one string on spaces, so a value in it can add arguments. The finding appears when request data (a servlet or Stapler request, a @RequestParam, @PathVariable or @QueryParameter value, Ktor's call.parameters ...) reaches the call inside one method (with a trace)."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Use ProcessBuilder with a fixed program and a list of arguments, check request values against an allowlist, and pass them after '--'. Never build a shell command string from request data.",
                "markdown": "**Why:** Runtime.getRuntime().exec() and new ProcessBuilder() start the program they are given. A request value that chooses the program, or reaches the script of 'sh -c' or 'cmd /c', runs commands of the attacker's choosing; Runtime.exec(String) also splits one string on spaces, so a value in it can add arguments. The finding appears when request data (a servlet or Stapler request, a @RequestParam, @PathVariable or @QueryParameter value, Ktor's call.parameters ...) reaches the call inside one method (with a trace).\n\n**Fix:** Use ProcessBuilder with a fixed program and a list of arguments, check request values against an allowlist, and pass them after '--'. Never build a shell command string from request data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Ruthvik-Bandari/kestrix/blob/main/docs/modules/code.md#rules",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "precision": "medium",
                "tags": [
