            {
              "id": "java.deserialize.unsafe",
              "name": "JavaDeserializeUnsafe",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Deserialization that lets the data choose the class (ObjectInputStream, XMLDecoder, XStream, Jackson default typing, SnakeYAML), Java and Kotlin"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "new ObjectInputStream() and new XMLDecoder() rebuild objects of whatever classes the stream names, and so do XStream.fromXML() without type permissions, Jackson with enableDefaultTyping/activateDefaultTyping or @JsonTypeInfo(use = Id.CLASS or MINIMAL_CLASS), and SnakeYAML's new Yaml() without a SafeConstructor (before 2.0). Bytes from an attacker can then run code through gadget classes on the class path. ObjectInputStream is not reported in a file that overrides resolveClass or sets an ObjectInputFilter, XStream not where allowTypes/addPermission is called, SnakeYAML not where a SafeConstructor or LoaderOptions appears."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Exchange data as JSON or another data-only format mapped to fixed classes. If Java serialization is unavoidable, set an ObjectInputFilter (jdk.serialFilter or ObjectInputStream.setObjectInputFilter) that allows only the expected classes; give XStream an allowlist of types; use Jackson without default typing or with a PolymorphicTypeValidator that allows named base types; construct SnakeYAML with a SafeConstructor.",
                "markdown": "**Why:** new ObjectInputStream() and new XMLDecoder() rebuild objects of whatever classes the stream names, and so do XStream.fromXML() without type permissions, Jackson with enableDefaultTyping/activateDefaultTyping or @JsonTypeInfo(use = Id.CLASS or MINIMAL_CLASS), and SnakeYAML's new Yaml() without a SafeConstructor (before 2.0). Bytes from an attacker can then run code through gadget classes on the class path. ObjectInputStream is not reported in a file that overrides resolveClass or sets an ObjectInputFilter, XStream not where allowTypes/addPermission is called, SnakeYAML not where a SafeConstructor or LoaderOptions appears.\n\n**Fix:** Exchange data as JSON or another data-only format mapped to fixed classes. If Java serialization is unavoidable, set an ObjectInputFilter (jdk.serialFilter or ObjectInputStream.setObjectInputFilter) that allows only the expected classes; give XStream an allowlist of types; use Jackson without default typing or with a PolymorphicTypeValidator that allows named base types; construct SnakeYAML with a SafeConstructor."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Ruthvik-Bandari/kestrix/blob/main/docs/modules/code.md#rules",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "precision": "medium",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-502"
                ]
              }
