                "text": "Start a fixed program and add request values to ProcessStartInfo.ArgumentList (one item per argument), after checking them against an allowlist; keep UseShellExecute false. Never build a 'cmd /c' or 'sh -c' string from request data.",
                "markdown": "**Why:** Process.Start(), new ProcessStartInfo() and its FileName and Arguments properties start the program they are given with an argument string that the program splits itself. A request value that chooses the program, reaches 'cmd.exe /c' or 'sh -c', or adds to the argument string can run other commands or add options.\n\n**Fix:** Start a fixed program and add request values to ProcessStartInfo.ArgumentList (one item per argument), after checking them against an allowlist; keep UseShellExecute false. Never build a 'cmd /c' or 'sh -c' string from request data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Ruthvik-Bandari/kestrix/blob/main/docs/modules/code.md#rules",
