            {
              "id": "cs.deserialize.unsafe",
              "name": "CsDeserializeUnsafe",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Deserializer that lets the data choose the type (BinaryFormatter, SoapFormatter, NetDataContractSerializer, LosFormatter, ObjectStateFormatter, Json.NET TypeNameHandling), C#"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BinaryFormatter, SoapFormatter, NetDataContractSerializer, LosFormatter and ObjectStateFormatter create whatever .NET types the payload names; Microsoft states BinaryFormatter cannot be made safe and removed it in .NET 9. Json.NET with TypeNameHandling other than None, and JavaScriptSerializer with a SimpleTypeResolver, do the same for JSON. A payload from an attacker can run code through gadget types. TypeNameHandling is not reported in a file that sets a SerializationBinder."
