              "help": {
                "text": "Use System.Text.Json or DataContractSerializer with known types, or Json.NET with TypeNameHandling.None. If type names are needed, set an ISerializationBinder that allows only your own types.",
                "markdown": "**Why:** BinaryFormatter, SoapFormatter, NetDataContractSerializer, LosFormatter and ObjectStateFormatter create whatever .NET types the payload names; Microsoft states BinaryFormatter cannot be made safe and removed it in .NET 9. Json.NET with TypeNameHandling other than None, and JavaScriptSerializer with a SimpleTypeResolver, do the same for JSON. A payload from an attacker can run code through gadget types. TypeNameHandling is not reported in a file that sets a SerializationBinder.\n\n**Fix:** Use System.Text.Json or DataContractSerializer with known types, or Json.NET with TypeNameHandling.None. If type names are needed, set an ISerializationBinder that allows only your own types."
              },
