            {
              "id": "cs.path.traversal",
              "name": "CsPathTraversal",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "File path built from request data, C#"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "File.ReadAllText, File.OpenRead, File.WriteAllBytes, File.Delete, the Directory methods, new FileStream(), new StreamReader(), PhysicalFile() and ExtractToFile() use the path they are given; Path.Combine keeps a rooted second argument and does not remove '..'. A request value, or the FullName of an archive entry (zip slip), can reach files outside the intended directory."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Use Path.GetFileName for a file name, or combine with a fixed root, call Path.GetFullPath, and check the result starts with the root (plus a directory separator) before opening it.",
                "markdown": "**Why:** File.ReadAllText, File.OpenRead, File.WriteAllBytes, File.Delete, the Directory methods, new FileStream(), new StreamReader(), PhysicalFile() and ExtractToFile() use the path they are given; Path.Combine keeps a rooted second argument and does not remove '..'. A request value, or the FullName of an archive entry (zip slip), can reach files outside the intended directory.\n\n**Fix:** Use Path.GetFileName for a file name, or combine with a fixed root, call Path.GetFullPath, and check the result starts with the root (plus a directory separator) before opening it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Ruthvik-Bandari/kestrix/blob/main/docs/modules/code.md#rules",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
