              }
            },
            {
              "id": "rb.exec.command",
              "name": "RbExecCommand",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Shell command built from request data, Ruby"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "system, exec, spawn, IO.popen, Open3.capture2/capture3/popen3 with one string, backticks and %x() pass the command to a shell. Request data interpolated into it can add ';', '&&' or '$(...)' and run other commands."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Pass the program and each argument separately (system('convert', path, out)), which runs without a shell, and check request values against an allowlist; Shellwords.escape when a shell string is unavoidable.",
                "markdown": "**Why:** system, exec, spawn, IO.popen, Open3.capture2/capture3/popen3 with one string, backticks and %x() pass the command to a shell. Request data interpolated into it can add ';', '&&' or '$(...)' and run other commands.\n\n**Fix:** Pass the program and each argument separately (system('convert', path, out)), which runs without a shell, and check request values against an allowlist; Shellwords.escape when a shell string is unavoidable."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Ruthvik-Bandari/kestrix/blob/main/docs/modules/code.md#rules",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
