            {
              "id": "rb.path.traversal",
              "name": "RbPathTraversal",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "File path built from request data, Ruby"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "File.read, File.open, File.write, IO.read, Dir.glob, the FileUtils methods, send_file and render file: use the path they are given. A request value with '../' or an absolute path in it reaches files outside the intended directory; File.join does not stop that."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Use File.basename for a file name, or expand the path against a fixed root (File.expand_path(name, root)) and check it starts with the root plus a separator before use; send files by a looked-up record rather than a request path.",
                "markdown": "**Why:** File.read, File.open, File.write, IO.read, Dir.glob, the FileUtils methods, send_file and render file: use the path they are given. A request value with '../' or an absolute path in it reaches files outside the intended directory; File.join does not stop that.\n\n**Fix:** Use File.basename for a file name, or expand the path against a fixed root (File.expand_path(name, root)) and check it starts with the root plus a separator before use; send files by a looked-up record rather than a request path."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/Ruthvik-Bandari/kestrix/blob/main/docs/modules/code.md#rules",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
